Package: peabiru
Title: Multimodal Routing on 'OpenStreetMap' and 'GTFS' Networks
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("André", "Leite", email = "leite@castlab.org", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4718-9766")),
    person("StrategicProjects", role = c("cph", "fnd"),
           comment = "Also copyright holder of the bundled Rust crate peabiru-core")
  )
Description: Computes travel-time matrices and accessibility on multimodal
    transport networks (walk, bike, car and public transport) built from
    'OpenStreetMap' extracts and 'GTFS' feeds. The functions, their arguments
    and their results are those of the 'r5r' package, whose routing engine
    'R5' this package reproduces exactly; the engine is written in 'Rust' and
    shared with the 'Python' package of the same name, and no 'Java' runtime
    is required.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.81
Config/rextendr/version: 0.5.0
Depends: 
    R (>= 4.2)
Suggests:
    r5r,
    sf,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
